From e2c8123c5f5f15b8f38b1ddaddb790111e196c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 16:25:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 75/75] fix(done): close review-only bead when its PR merged
 mid-close (gfork-21p)

Add a "PR already MERGED -> close cleanly" short-circuit to the review-only
close gate, before the "no fresh review evidence" escalation. This is the
PR-merge-completes-during-close variant, distinct from 0070's renovate-rebase
variant (feryn-5sa6).

Root cause: when a PR merges DURING `gt done` (observed merge and escalate ~1s
apart), two checks break together. currentReviewEvidenceHead() reads the
reviewer's LOCAL worktree HEAD, which has advanced to the merge commit and no
longer matches the approved PR head, so the head-anchored bead-comment evidence
check misses. The reviewOnlyPRHasFreshDecision() GitHub fallback then races
merge finalization and fails safe to false. Together they emit a spurious
"ESCALATE: review-only close loop <id>" for a review that plainly succeeded.

A merged PR trivially proves the review passed: merge safety is enforced
INDEPENDENTLY by the merge gate (git.IsPullRequestApproved / refinery
rejectMRBeforeMerge), so review-only close does not need strict fresh evidence
once the PR is merged. New git.IsPullRequestMerged queries PR state directly
(mirrors HasReviewDecisionSince, no target-repo resolution); reviewOnlyPRMerged
wires it into the gate via the attached pr_url and fails safe to escalate on any
absent-URL / cwd / gh error. CHANGES_REQUESTED PRs never reach MERGED, so that
gate is intact.

Tests (red->green verified): a review-only bead whose PR merges during close
(head advanced to the merge commit, no fresh evidence, decision query races to
empty) now CLOSES instead of escalating; an unmerged PR with no evidence still
escalates. Both fail against the pre-fix gate for the right reason.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
